{
  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_011 (scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) is the clear best at 0.6776 acc / 0.6464 F1, far ahead of all other configs. The dominant factor appears to be the RNA encoder (scvi_n200 >> pca_n2000 > scgpt). With pca_n2000, resnet50 and imagenet_vit_l performed nearly identically (0.6390 vs 0.6352), so the image encoder's contribution is unresolved. Question: Does pairing the strongest RNA representation (scvi_n200) with the stronger image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) yield further gains, or is resnet50 already sufficient? config_007 changes only the image encoder (resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l) relative to config_011, keeping scvi_n200, avgpool, weighted, and multiprofile fixed. This is the cleanest single-variable test to determine whether the image modality is currently the bottleneck or whether the RNA encoder is the primary driver. Under a limited budget, confirming or refuting the image-encoder interaction with the best RNA encoder is more informative than re-testing aggregation or fusion, for which we already have directional evidence."
}

